    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56-a8">

                <pb facs="0117" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg67"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">note of the portuguese legation to the brazilian
                        government.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Portuguese Legation in Brazil</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge your note No. 13, dated 15th March, and which
                    reached me on the 16th at 9:30 p.m., relative to the admission of the insurgents
                    on board the Portuguese men-of-war. I note that your excellency demands the
                    surrender of those people, and await the orders of my Government in this
                    respect; and must assure you that on this morning I have given orders to the
                    commander of the <hi rendition="#italic">Mindello</hi> not to land them on
                    foreign soil, and that he must keep them aboard till the final solution of the
                    diplomatic question.</p>
                <p>I assure you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conde Paraty</hi>,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To Dr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassiano do Nascimento</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign Affairs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
